---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="synterr-nlp"
  description="Open Russian grammatical error correction. Rule-grounded synthetic data, per-rule diagnostics, reproducible pipelines."
  wide={true}
>
  <!-- Hero: the product demonstrates itself before any claim ----------- -->
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Grammatical error correction,<br />evaluated honestly.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Most GEC benchmarks summarize heterogeneous behavior into one F-score
      and miss the parts where models silently regress. We build the
      rule-grounded synthetic data and per-rule diagnostics that surface
      what aggregate metrics hide. Currently focused on Russian.
    </p>

    <figure class="specimen-fig">
      <p class="specimen" lang="ru">
        Мы гуляли в&nbsp;<span class="edit"><del>лесе</del><ins>лесу</ins></span>&nbsp;весь день.
      </p>
      <figcaption class="specimen-caption">
        Real output: synterr corrupts clean text into a second-locative error
        and labels it — <span class="tag">noun_case_prep_e_u</span>
        <span class="para-ref">§152</span> — one of 75&nbsp;error types placed
        by the dependency tree, not by chance.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="hero-cta">
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/papers/bea-2026/overview/">Read the BEA 2026 overview</a>
      <a class="cta-link" href="https://github.com/synterr-nlp/synterr" rel="external">Code on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Featured paper: the one red band --------------------------------- -->
  <section class="band">
    <p class="band-kicker">Accepted at ACL BEA 2026</p>
    <h2 class="band-title">What Aggregate Scores Hide</h2>
    <p class="band-blurb">
      Across eight open models from 0.8B to 12B parameters, fine-tuning on
      synthetic data <em>raises</em> overall F<sub>0.5</sub> on LoRuGEC —
      while driving subordinate-clause comma accuracy from
      <strong>14% to 1%</strong>. Aggregate scores can't detect this;
      per-rule diagnostics can. Once detected, it's fixable.
    </p>
    <p class="band-links">
      <a href="/papers/bea-2026/overview/">graphical overview</a>
      <a href="/papers/bea-2026/">paper landing</a>
      <a href="/papers/bea-2026/tables/per-rule/">per-rule data</a>
      <a href="/papers/bea-2026/tables/reasoning-9b/">reasoning chains</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- The ledger: what we make, cited like Rozental cites rules -------- -->
  <section class="ledger">
    <article class="entry">
      <div class="entry-ref"><span class="para-ref">§ 1</span></div>
      <div class="entry-body">
        <h3>Synterr, the generator</h3>
        <p>
          An open-source synthetic-error generator for Russian: 28 handlers,
          75 error types, each grounded in the dependency tree and mapped to
          a 100-category taxonomy from Rozental's reference grammar. Errors
          carry their rule — filter, re-weight, and audit by it.
        </p>
        <p class="entry-links">
          <a href="/synterr/">docs</a> · <a href="https://github.com/synterr-nlp/synterr" rel="external">github</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="entry">
      <div class="entry-ref"><span class="para-ref">§ 2</span></div>
      <div class="entry-body">
        <h3>Per-rule diagnostics</h3>
        <p>
          A browsable taxonomy and per-rule scores for evaluating Russian
          GEC systems honestly. Cell-coloured xlsx parsed natively in your
          browser — sortable, filterable, downloadable.
        </p>
        <p class="entry-links">
          <a href="/papers/bea-2026/tables/cross-reference/">browse the taxonomy</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="entry">
      <div class="entry-ref"><span class="para-ref">§ 3</span></div>
      <div class="entry-body">
        <h3>Reproducible pipelines</h3>
        <p>
          Every released dataset ships with a pinned generation commit,
          SHA-256 checksums, and a verifier script. The v4 SFT data is
          byte-verified against the file the paper trained on.
        </p>
        <p class="entry-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/synterr-nlp/synterr/blob/master/data/V4_DATA_PROVENANCE.md" rel="external">v4 provenance</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <!-- Anatomy: the dependency-tree grounding ---------------------------- -->
  <section class="anatomy">
    <figure class="anatomy-fig">
      <img src="/papers/bea-2026/figures/depparse_errors.svg"
           alt="A Russian sentence with three rule-grounded error sites annotated on its dependency tree." />
    </figure>
    <div class="anatomy-text">
      <h2>Errors are placed by the parse, not by chance.</h2>
      <p>
        Three rule-grounded error sites on one sentence: agreement
        (<code>amod</code>), a subordinate-clause boundary
        (<code>acl:relcl</code>), case government (<code>obl</code>).
        Handlers fire only where the dependency tree licenses the error —
        and refuse where the "corruption" would be correct Russian,
        so a non-error never enters the training data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Recent ------------------------------------------------------------ -->
  <section class="activity">
    <h2 class="activity-title">Recent</h2>
    <ul class="timeline">
      <li>
        <time datetime="2026-05-14">2026-05-14</time>
        <span><strong>Synterr v1.0.1 on Zenodo.</strong> Archived at <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20182862" rel="external">10.5281/zenodo.20182862</a>.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <time datetime="2026-05-09">2026-05-09</time>
        <span><strong>Site online.</strong> Browsable tables, reasoning-chain viewer, graphical overview.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <time datetime="2026-05-04">2026-05-04</time>
        <span><strong>BEA 2026 acceptance.</strong> "What Aggregate Scores Hide" accepted at the 21st BEA workshop.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <time datetime="2026-05-01">2026-05-01</time>
        <span><strong>Synterr v1.0.</strong> Paper release with reproducibility pack (checksums, verify script, pinned commit).</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <time datetime="2026-03-22">2026-03-22</time>
        <span><strong>v4 dataset frozen.</strong> 39,209 SFT examples, deterministic build pipeline.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .hero {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 4.5rem;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 5.2vw, 3.4rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
  }
  .hero .lede {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.62;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin: 0 0 2.8rem;
  }

  /* The specimen: a real corruption, marked like a proofreader would */
  .specimen-fig {
    margin: 0 0 2.6rem;
  }
  .specimen {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.3rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem; /* room for the caret below the baseline */
    padding-top: 0.9em; /* room for the interline insertion */
  }
  .specimen-caption {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 38rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  /* load choreography: strike draws, then the correction rises */
  .specimen del::after {
    animation: strike 0.32s var(--ease-out) 0.45s backwards;
  }
  .specimen .edit ins,
  .specimen .edit::after {
    animation: rise 0.24s var(--ease-out) 0.85s backwards;
  }
  @keyframes strike {
    from { transform: scaleX(0); }
    to   { transform: scaleX(1); }
  }
  @keyframes rise {
    from { opacity: 0; translate: 0 0.25em; }
    to   { opacity: 1; translate: 0 0; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .specimen del::after,
    .specimen .edit ins,
    .specimen .edit::after { animation: none; }
  }

  .hero-cta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .btn-primary {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.15rem;
    background: var(--red);
    color: var(--on-red);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--bg);
  }
  .cta-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  /* ── The red band ─────────────────────────────────────── */
  .band {
    background: var(--red);
    color: var(--on-red);
    padding: 2.4rem 2.6rem 2.5rem;
    margin: 0 0 4.5rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .band-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
  .band-title {
    color: inherit;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.4vw, 2.2rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
  }
  .band-blurb {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
  }
  .band-blurb strong {
    font-weight: 700;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .band-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.6rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .band a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    text-decoration-color: color-mix(in oklab, currentColor 55%, transparent);
  }
  .band a:hover { text-decoration-color: currentColor; }

  /* ── The ledger ───────────────────────────────────────── */
  .ledger {
    margin: 0 0 5rem;
  }
  .entry {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5.5rem 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.8rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .entry:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .entry-ref .para-ref {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  .entry-body h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin: -0.2rem 0 0.55rem;
  }
  .entry-body p {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 42rem;
  }
  .entry-links {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  /* ── Anatomy ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .anatomy {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.25fr 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin: 0 0 5rem;
  }
  .anatomy-fig img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    background: #fff;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .anatomy-text h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
  }
  .anatomy-text p {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.62;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Activity ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .activity-title {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .timeline {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .timeline li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7.5rem 1fr;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .timeline time {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--red);
    padding-top: 0.15rem;
  }
  .timeline span { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .timeline strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 650; }

  /* ── Responsive ───────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .hero { margin-top: 1.2rem; }
    .band { padding: 1.8rem 1.4rem 1.9rem; }
    .entry { grid-template-columns: 3.2rem 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
    .anatomy { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.6rem; }
    .timeline li { grid-template-columns: 6rem 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  }
</style>
